@startuml
title SysML BDD - Movement Task System

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class "MovementTaskSystem" as System <<block>> {
  +assign task
  +execute task
  +advance plan
  +report status
}

class "Mission UI" as UI <<block>> {
  +task menu
  +task dialog
  +plan dialog
  +graphics editor
}

class "Plan Execution" as Plan <<block>> {
  +EntityPlanExecutor
  +PlanStep
  +PlanStepKind
}

class "Scenario Runtime" as Runtime <<block>> {
  +ScenarioState
  +SimulationEngine
  +FlightDynamicsEngine
}

class "Task Assignment" as Assignment <<block>> {
  +TaskApplicator
  +AssignTaskController
  +TaskAssignmentController
}

class "Task Primitives" as Primitives <<block>> {
  +MoveToLocationTask
  +FollowEntityTask
  +InterceptEntity3DTask
  +RouteTask
  +TaskStack
}

class "Tactical Graphics" as Graphics <<block>> {
  +Waypoint
  +RouteGraphic
  +RoutePoint
  +AreaDefinition
}

class "Persistence" as Persistence <<block>> {
  +ScenarioSerializer
  +scenario_state.json
}

class "Operational Status" as Status <<block>> {
  +EntityStatusFormatter
  +TrackSummaryBuilder
}

System *-- UI
System *-- Plan
System *-- Runtime
System *-- Assignment
System *-- Primitives
System *-- Graphics
System *-- Persistence
System *-- Status

UI --> Assignment : task request
UI --> Plan : plan authoring
UI --> Graphics : create/edit waypoint/route
Plan --> Assignment : start active step
Assignment --> Runtime : persist EntityTask
Assignment --> Primitives : build TaskStack primitive
Runtime --> Primitives : evaluate every tick
Runtime --> Plan : currentTask.status
Runtime --> Persistence : save/load
Status --> Runtime : read entity state

note bottom of Primitives
Visible movement capabilities:
- Follow Entity
- Intercept Entity
- Follow Route
- Move To Location / Waypoint
- Return To Base
end note

@enduml
